# Odo auto-land verify gate (M16 / O-1 v2).
# The daemon runs the FIRST non-comment line as a shell command at a run's
# worktree root; a diff may land without a human only if it exits 0.
# Diffs touching THIS file are blocked by the supply-chain gate (self-
# modification always requires a human).
#
# Path-scoped verify (Fix 3, scope-union since diff #9): a glob-prefixed
# line runs whenever the diff TOUCHES that scope (>=1 path matches); the
# bare fallback line additionally runs when any diff path sits outside
# every glob's scope. A mixed go+gui diff therefore runs BOTH commands.
#
# vitest runs capped at --maxWorkers=2 ONLY here (pitfall #42 family,
# 2026-09-01: verify's vitest segment flaked act/timing-sensitive tests
# under full parallelism — every failure passed isolated and in warm local
# runs). vitest.config.ts stays untouched so dev/test runs keep full
# parallelism; no --retry: the worker cap is the honest fix, a retry would
# only mask a real flake.
gui/**: cd gui && npx tsc --noEmit && npx vitest run --maxWorkers=2 && npx playwright test --reporter=line --retries=1
go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test -timeout=20m ./...
